diff -ruN 05-ui/docs/monitoring/slo.md 06-monitoring/docs/monitoring/slo.md
--- 05-ui/docs/monitoring/slo.md	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ 06-monitoring/docs/monitoring/slo.md	2026-11-22 20:27:09
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Service Level Objective
+
+<!-- TODO(team): agree the target numbers below; keep queries/slo-windows*.kql in sync. -->
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| **User journey** | "Show me when I can leave": `GET /passages/{id}/windows` on the API |
+| **SLI** | Share of those requests that answer with a status below 500 **and** in under 1000 ms |
+| **Objective** | **99%** over a rolling **1 hour** window |
+| **Error budget** | 1% of requests per hour may be slow or fail |
+| **Measured by** | [queries/slo-windows.kql](queries/slo-windows.kql) (current value) and [queries/slo-windows-trend.kql](queries/slo-windows-trend.kql) (trend) |
+
+## Why this journey
+
+It is the feature beyond CRUD and the only request that crosses both services and the external
+API, so it is the first thing to break and the one users care about.
+
+## Why 503 counts as bad
+
+When the forecast service is down the API answers fast with a clear `503 degraded` message
+(see [../partial-failure.md](../partial-failure.md)). That is the correct behaviour, but the user
+still did not get their windows, so it burns error budget.
+
+## Known risks to the objective
+
+- **Scale to zero.** Both Container Apps scale to zero (brief §4). The first request after an idle
+  period waits for a cold start, and Azure SQL serverless may also need up to a minute to resume.
+  With little demo traffic this alone can break a 1-hour objective.
+- **Cache misses.** A new location means two Open-Meteo calls per point. Repeat requests hit the
+  forecast service's cache and are much faster.
+
+## What we do when the budget is spent
+
+Look at tile 6 (upstream health) and `recent-errors.kql` first; then check the Container Apps
+revision and recent deploys. Feature work pauses until the SLI is back above the objective.
diff -ruN 05-ui/docs/partial-failure.md 06-monitoring/docs/partial-failure.md
--- 05-ui/docs/partial-failure.md	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ 06-monitoring/docs/partial-failure.md	2026-11-22 20:28:36
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Partial-failure test
+
+Brief §6: *"with one service down (or an external API failing), the other keeps working and the
+affected flow fails with a timeout and a clear message, not a stack trace or a hung request."*
+
+The test is a script, so anyone can repeat it: `scripts/partial-failure.sh`. It exits `0` when
+every check passes and always restores the system, even if interrupted.
+
+## What protects us
+
+| Failure | Where it is handled | What the user gets |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Forecast service down or slow | `services/api/app/forecast_client.py` (10 s timeout) and `routers/windows.py` | `503 {"status": "degraded", "detail": "Forecast unavailable: … Boats and passages still work…"}`. Boats and passages keep working. The UI shows the message in a banner. |
+| Open-Meteo down or slow | `services/forecast/app/openmeteo.py` (4 s timeout) and `service.py` | The last cached forecast, marked `"stale": true`, or a `503` with a clear reason when nothing is cached. |
+| Azure SQL paused or unreachable | `app/db.py` (startup retries, `pool_pre_ping`) and the `OperationalError` handler in `app/main.py` | `503 "Database unavailable, please retry in a few seconds."` |
+
+Automated tests cover each path without Docker:
+`services/api/tests/test_windows.py::test_forecast_failure_gives_clear_degraded_response`,
+`test_crud_keeps_working_while_forecast_is_down`, and `services/forecast/tests/test_forecast.py`
+(`timeout`, `http500`, `stale` cases).
+
+## Scenario A: the forecast service is stopped (local)
+
+```bash
+docker compose up -d --build
+scripts/partial-failure.sh
+```
+
+Steps the script performs and checks:
+
+1. Baseline: `GET /passages/{id}/windows` returns `200`.
+2. `docker compose stop forecast`.
+3. `GET /passages/{id}/windows` returns **503** with `status: degraded` in **well under 15 s**
+   and no stack trace. `GET /boats` returns 200; `POST /boats` still creates a boat.
+4. `docker compose start forecast` and wait for `/health`.
+5. Windows return `200` again.
+
+Expected output (recorded 2026-11-22 on a laptop):
+
+```text
+3. Checks while it is down
+  windows answered HTTP 503 in 0.008383s: Forecast unavailable: forecast service is unreachable (ConnectError). Boats and passages still work; try the windows again in a minute.
+  PASS  windows returns 503, not 500
+  PASS  body says status=degraded
+  PASS  answered in under 15s (no hung request)
+  PASS  no stack trace in the response
+  PASS  GET /boats still 200
+  PASS  POST /boats still works (id 4)
+...
+RESULT: PASS
+```
+
+## Scenario B: Open-Meteo is unreachable (local)
+
+```bash
+scripts/partial-failure.sh upstream
+```
+
+The script restarts the forecast service with `OPEN_METEO_MARINE_URL` pointing at an unroutable
+address, so every upstream call hits the 4 s timeout. A location that was never cached returns a
+clear `503` (`"open-meteo-marine did not answer within 4s; no cached data for this location"`);
+a cached passage still gets its windows from the cache (marked stale once the cache entry is older
+than 30 minutes). Then it restores the normal URL.
+
+## Scenario C: in Azure (for the Sprint Review)
+
+Run it against the deployed system (needs `az login` with access to the resource group). It disables
+ingress on the forecast Container App for about a minute and re-enables it on exit.
+
+```bash
+API_URL=https://<api-fqdn> FORECAST_URL=https://<forecast-fqdn> \
+RESOURCE_GROUP=rg-sdd-3a-g<N> PREFIX=sdd-3a-g<N> \
+scripts/partial-failure.sh azure
+```
+
+While it runs, open the UI: the planner shows the red "Forecast unavailable" banner while the
+Boats and Passages pages keep working. Afterwards, `docs/monitoring/queries/error-rate.kql` and
+`upstream-health.kql` show the spike. The next CD run puts the ingress back in its declared state
+anyway (infra is re-applied from Bicep on every deploy).
diff -ruN 05-ui/scripts/partial-failure.sh 06-monitoring/scripts/partial-failure.sh
--- 05-ui/scripts/partial-failure.sh	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ 06-monitoring/scripts/partial-failure.sh	2026-11-22 20:27:45
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Repeatable partial-failure test (brief §6). See docs/partial-failure.md.
+#
+#   scripts/partial-failure.sh              forecast service stopped (local, docker compose)
+#   scripts/partial-failure.sh upstream     Open-Meteo unreachable (local, docker compose)
+#   scripts/partial-failure.sh azure        forecast service unreachable in Azure (needs az login)
+#
+# Exit code 0 = every check passed. The system is always restored at the end.
+set -uo pipefail
+
+MODE="${1:-forecast}"
+API_URL="${API_URL:-http://localhost:8010}"
+FORECAST_URL="${FORECAST_URL:-http://localhost:8011}"
+MAX_SECONDS="${MAX_SECONDS:-15}"   # the degraded answer must come back faster than this
+FAILURES=0
+
+pass() { echo "  PASS  $*"; }
+fail() { echo "  FAIL  $*"; FAILURES=$((FAILURES + 1)); }
+need() { command -v "$1" >/dev/null || { echo "needs $1"; exit 2; }; }
+need curl; need python3
+
+field() { python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('$1',''))" 2>/dev/null; }
+
+wait_for() { # url seconds
+  for ((s = 0; s < $2; s += 2)); do curl -sf -m 5 "$1" >/dev/null && return 0; sleep 2; done
+  return 1
+}
+
+demo_passage() {
+  local id
+  id=$(curl -sf -m 20 "$API_URL/passages" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d[0]["id"] if d else "")')
+  if [[ -z "$id" ]]; then
+    local boat
+    boat=$(curl -sf -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+      -d '{"name":"Failure-test boat","max_wind_kn":20,"max_wave_m":2}' "$API_URL/boats" | field id)
+    id=$(curl -sf -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+      -d "{\"name\":\"Failure-test passage\",\"boat_id\":$boat,\"start_lat\":41.37,\"start_lon\":2.19,\"end_lat\":41.23,\"end_lon\":1.81,\"speed_kn\":6}" \
+      "$API_URL/passages" | field id)
+  fi
+  echo "$id"
+}
+
+check_degraded() { # passage_id
+  local out code secs body
+  out=$(curl -s -m 60 -w '\n%{http_code} %{time_total}' "$API_URL/passages/$1/windows")
+  body=$(echo "$out" | sed '$d'); read -r code secs <<<"$(echo "$out" | tail -1)"
+  echo "  windows answered HTTP $code in ${secs}s: $(echo "$body" | field detail)"
+  [[ "$code" == "503" ]] && pass "windows returns 503, not 500" || fail "expected 503, got $code"
+  [[ "$(echo "$body" | field status)" == "degraded" ]] && pass "body says status=degraded" || fail "no status=degraded in body"
+  python3 -c "import sys; sys.exit(0 if float('$secs') < $MAX_SECONDS else 1)" \
+    && pass "answered in under ${MAX_SECONDS}s (no hung request)" || fail "took ${secs}s"
+  echo "$body" | grep -q 'Traceback' && fail "stack trace leaked" || pass "no stack trace in the response"
+}
+
+check_crud_still_works() {
+  [[ "$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 20 "$API_URL/boats")" == "200" ]] \
+    && pass "GET /boats still 200" || fail "GET /boats broken"
+  local id
+  id=$(curl -s -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+    -d '{"name":"Created while degraded","max_wind_kn":15,"max_wave_m":1.5}' "$API_URL/boats" | field id)
+  if [[ -n "$id" ]]; then
+    pass "POST /boats still works (id $id)"
+    curl -s -o /dev/null -m 20 -X DELETE "$API_URL/boats/$id"
+  else
+    fail "POST /boats broken"
+  fi
+}
+
+echo "Partial-failure test: mode=$MODE"
+wait_for "$API_URL/health" 60 || { echo "API not up at $API_URL"; exit 2; }
+PID=$(demo_passage)
+echo "Using passage $PID"
+
+echo "1. Baseline"
+code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 60 "$API_URL/passages/$PID/windows")
+[[ "$code" == "200" ]] && pass "windows 200 before the failure" || fail "baseline windows answered $code"
+
+case "$MODE" in
+  forecast)
+    echo "2. Stop the forecast service"
+    trap 'docker compose start forecast >/dev/null 2>&1' EXIT
+    docker compose stop forecast >/dev/null 2>&1
+    echo "3. Checks while it is down"
+    check_degraded "$PID"
+    check_crud_still_works
+    echo "4. Restore"
+    docker compose start forecast >/dev/null 2>&1
+    wait_for "$FORECAST_URL/health" 90 && pass "forecast service back" || fail "forecast did not come back"
+    ;;
+  upstream)
+    echo "2. Point the forecast service at an unroutable Open-Meteo (requests time out)"
+    trap 'docker compose up -d forecast >/dev/null 2>&1' EXIT
+    OPEN_METEO_MARINE_URL="http://10.255.255.1/v1/marine" docker compose up -d forecast >/dev/null 2>&1
+    wait_for "$FORECAST_URL/health" 90 || fail "forecast did not restart"
+    echo "3. Checks while Open-Meteo is unreachable"
+    # A location never seen before has no cache: expect a clear 503 from the forecast service.
+    out=$(curl -s -m 60 -w '\n%{http_code}' "$FORECAST_URL/current?lat=12.34&lon=-45.67")
+    [[ "$(echo "$out" | tail -1)" == "503" ]] && pass "uncached location: 503 '$(echo "$out" | sed '$d' | field detail)'" \
+      || fail "uncached location did not return 503"
+    # The demo passage was cached by the baseline call: the stale copy can be served.
+    code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 60 "$API_URL/passages/$PID/windows")
+    [[ "$code" == "200" || "$code" == "503" ]] && pass "windows answered $code (200 = from cache, 503 = degraded)" \
+      || fail "windows answered $code"
+    check_crud_still_works
+    echo "4. Restore"
+    docker compose up -d forecast >/dev/null 2>&1
+    wait_for "$FORECAST_URL/health" 90 && pass "forecast service restored" || fail "forecast did not come back"
+    ;;
+  azure)
+    need az
+    : "${RESOURCE_GROUP:?set RESOURCE_GROUP, e.g. rg-sdd-3a-g3}" "${PREFIX:?set PREFIX, e.g. sdd-3a-g3}"
+    APP="$PREFIX-forecast"
+    echo "2. Disable ingress on $APP (temporary; restored on exit)"
+    trap 'az containerapp ingress enable -n "$APP" -g "$RESOURCE_GROUP" --type external --target-port 8000 --transport auto >/dev/null' EXIT
+    az containerapp ingress disable -n "$APP" -g "$RESOURCE_GROUP" >/dev/null
+    sleep 20
+    echo "3. Checks while it is unreachable"
+    check_degraded "$PID"
+    check_crud_still_works
+    echo "4. Restore"
+    az containerapp ingress enable -n "$APP" -g "$RESOURCE_GROUP" --type external --target-port 8000 --transport auto >/dev/null
+    trap - EXIT
+    pass "ingress re-enabled"
+    ;;
+  *) echo "unknown mode $MODE"; exit 2 ;;
+esac
+
+echo "5. After recovery"
+sleep 2
+code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 60 "$API_URL/passages/$PID/windows")
+[[ "$code" == "200" ]] && pass "windows 200 again" || fail "windows answered $code after recovery"
+
+echo
+if [[ $FAILURES -eq 0 ]]; then echo "RESULT: PASS"; else echo "RESULT: FAIL ($FAILURES checks)"; fi
+exit $FAILURES
diff -ruN 05-ui/scripts/traffic.sh 06-monitoring/scripts/traffic.sh
--- 05-ui/scripts/traffic.sh	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ 06-monitoring/scripts/traffic.sh	2026-11-22 20:27:51
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Generate demo traffic so the monitoring dashboard and SLO have data.
+#
+#   scripts/traffic.sh [ROUNDS]          default 50 rounds
+#   API_URL=... FORECAST_URL=... scripts/traffic.sh 200
+#
+# Each round: health checks, list boats/passages, the windows of every passage, current
+# conditions, and one request that is expected to 404 (so the error panels are not flat zero).
+# Creates a demo boat + passage if there are none. Read-only otherwise.
+set -euo pipefail
+
+API_URL="${API_URL:-http://localhost:8010}"
+FORECAST_URL="${FORECAST_URL:-http://localhost:8011}"
+ROUNDS="${1:-50}"
+PAUSE="${PAUSE:-0.5}"
+CODES_FILE=$(mktemp)
+trap 'rm -f "$CODES_FILE"' EXIT
+
+call() { # method url [json]
+  local code
+  if [[ $# -ge 3 ]]; then
+    code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 20 -X "$1" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$3" "$2" || true)
+  else
+    code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 20 -X "$1" "$2" || true)
+  fi
+  echo "$code" >>"$CODES_FILE"
+}
+
+json_ids() { python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(" ".join(str(x["id"]) for x in json.load(sys.stdin)))'; }
+
+echo "API:      $API_URL"
+echo "Forecast: $FORECAST_URL"
+curl -sf -m 60 "$API_URL/health" >/dev/null || { echo "API is not answering /health"; exit 1; }
+
+passages=$(curl -sf -m 20 "$API_URL/passages" | json_ids)
+if [[ -z "$passages" ]]; then
+  echo "No passages yet: creating a demo boat and passage."
+  boat=$(curl -sf -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+    -d '{"name":"Demo yacht","max_wind_kn":20,"max_gust_kn":28,"max_wave_m":2}' "$API_URL/boats" \
+    | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)["id"])')
+  curl -sf -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+    -d "{\"name\":\"Demo: Barcelona to Sitges\",\"boat_id\":$boat,\"start_lat\":41.37,\"start_lon\":2.19,\"end_lat\":41.23,\"end_lon\":1.81,\"speed_kn\":6}" \
+    "$API_URL/passages" >/dev/null
+  passages=$(curl -sf -m 20 "$API_URL/passages" | json_ids)
+fi
+
+for ((i = 1; i <= ROUNDS; i++)); do
+  call GET "$API_URL/health"
+  call GET "$FORECAST_URL/health"
+  call GET "$API_URL/boats"
+  call GET "$API_URL/passages"
+  for id in $passages; do call GET "$API_URL/passages/$id/windows"; done
+  call GET "$FORECAST_URL/current?lat=41.37&lon=2.19"
+  call GET "$API_URL/passages/999999"   # expected 404
+  printf '\rround %d/%d' "$i" "$ROUNDS"
+  sleep "$PAUSE"
+done
+echo
+echo "Status codes (count, code):"
+sort "$CODES_FILE" | uniq -c
